# Concrete C-c package and launch review

Review only after the independently approved preparation driver has actually returned a package. This review is read-only, limited to actual prepared artifacts, their pinned source callpaths, and the saved exact launch command. No tests, imports, driver rerun, synthetic probes, credentials/.env/environment values, Docker/provider/evaluation/campaign activity, or historical archive mutation.

Authenticate the actual preparation report and its manifest/config/policy references against the final P1-P4 source authority, updated readiness and driver approval. Check actual campaign/root/owner/tool/data/evaluator/image/source pins, finite limits, fresh absence of enrollment/launch/start/roles/reservations and no operational state copied from actual06. Inspect the actual initial investigator canonical request, wire messages and schema: allowed source/evidence categories, no raw market rows or secrets, parent provenance and metric ordering, exact byte/hash/token accounting within 75000 including output8192. Later author/critic packets remain response dependent and have not been fabricated.

Check the exact saved launch envelope against native rendered argv: physical Python, -B, native campaign command/flags from argv index4, exact artifact/config/manifest/policy/owner references; existing awake helper then credential helper then canonical CLI campaign dispatch. The workspace import path must be explicit without modifying executor-bound environment values. No old campaign-specific helper may substitute or omit policy arguments. Authenticate helper/parser source hashes. Credential resolution happens only after the fresh grant. AC and lid open remain operator conditions; the awake helper prevents idle sleep only.

Check the proposed grant: target two actual evaluated feedback rounds with critic/checkpoint/cleanup, at most three lifecycle attempts/eight role calls/600000 total tokens, 75000 prospective per role, output8192, retry0/repair0, original six-hour campaign wall deadline, native phase and cleanup limits, development-only scope, model identifier openai/gpt-5.4, no price quote and no hard USD ceiling. One two-call rejection can fit with two three-call evaluated rounds; actual model and runtime outcomes are not guaranteed. Report failed/rejected versus evaluated counts separately. Native policy admission enforces remaining reserve and fails on identity or policy mismatch; do not refresh authority or deadline to keep running.

Review the concrete observation plan: one actual exec session, retained stdout/result metadata, polls of that same session only, no duplicate launch after an observation timeout, native targeted cleanup authority, and no automatic restart/regrant when a terminal failure or insufficient reserve prevents the milestone. Verify exact current files before grant and again before launch. Docker daemon/image liveness and provider availability remain unexecuted; do not claim them verified. No Docker image pull or rebuild is authorized by this package.

Write a separate concrete-c-c-independent-review.md with exact package/launch hashes, spec and quality verdicts, concrete findings and any material unresolved risks. Approval makes the package ready for a fresh user paid-run grant; it is not that grant and does not authorize execution. Do not reopen already approved historical/source work without a concrete new discrepancy.
